# sapintegrationsuite_api_product (Resource)

An API product bundles one or more API proxies into what application developers find and
subscribe to in the API business hub enterprise, with an optional quota and OAuth scopes.
Proxies do the work; the product decides who may call them and how often.

**Status:** supported. Backed by `APIProducts` of the API portal's `Management.svc`; create,
read and delete were run on a tenant.

## Prerequisites

- The `api_management` block in the provider configuration, with the role
  `APIPortal.Administrator`.
- At least one API proxy, for example from [`sapintegrationsuite_api_proxy`](api_proxy.md). SAP
  refuses a product without one.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the product with its linked proxies and additional properties in one request. `status_code` defaults to `PUBLISHED`; `DRAFT` creates an unpublished product. |
| Read | Reads the product, its linked proxies and its additional properties, so drift in each is detected. |
| Update | None. SAP answers every update of a product (`PUT`, `PATCH`, `MERGE`) with 405. |
| Replacement | **Any change** deletes the product and creates it again. Applications subscribed to the old product lose that subscription. Read plans that replace a product carefully. |
| Delete | Deletes the product. |

